step	1	-	After starting the quest
line	<col=000080>I spoke to <col=800000>Farmer Bea</col> south west of the <col=800000>Digsite</col> and agreed to help her set up her <col=800000>Bee Farm</col>. To do so, I need to head to the <col=800000>Grand Exchange</col> in <col=800000>Varrock</col> and collect some <col=800000>Bees</col> from a <col=800000>Bee Dealer</col> there. I should be able to find him near the east entrance to the <col=800000>Exchange</col>.</col>
step	2	-	After collecting the bees
line	<str>I spoke to Farmer Bea south west of the Digsite and agreed to help her set up her Bee Farm.</str>
line	<col=000080>At <col=800000>Bea's</col> request, I travelled to the <col=800000>Grand Exchange</col> in <col=800000>Varrock</col> and collected some <col=800000>Bees</col> from a <col=800000>Bee Dealer</col> there. I should carefully transport them back to <col=800000>Bea</col>.</col>
step	3	-	Hunting the wasps
line	<str>I spoke to Farmer Bea south west of the Digsite and agreed to help her set up her Bee Farm.</str>
line	<str>The bee dealer gave me a box of bees. I should transport them safely back to Farmer Bea at her farm west of The Digsite.</str>
line	<str>At Bea's request, I travelled to the Grand Exchange in Varrock and collected some Bees from a Bee Dealer there. I then carefully delivered them to Bea. However, upon taking them to her hives, we discovered them to actually be Wasps.</str>
line	<col=000080><col=800000>Bea</col> asked me to thin down the number of <col=800000>Wasps</col> by catching 50 of them and bringing her back proof. If needed, <col=800000>Bea</col> has a crate of equipment that I can use for catching them.</col>
step	4	-	Delivering the stingers
line	<str>I spoke to Farmer Bea south west of the Digsite and agreed to help her set up her Bee Farm.</str>
line	<str>The bee dealer gave me a box of bees. I should transport them safely back to Farmer Bea at her farm west of The Digsite.</str>
line	<str>At Bea's request, I travelled to the Grand Exchange in Varrock and collected some Bees from a Bee Dealer there. I then carefully delivered them to Bea. However, upon taking them to her hives, we discovered them to actually be Wasps.</str>
line	<col=000080><col=800000>Bea</col> asked me to thin down the number of <col=800000>Wasps</col> by catching 50 of them. I did so and gathered 50 <col=800000>Wasp Stingers</col> in the process. I should show them to <col=800000>Bea</col>.</col>
step	5	-	Hunting the birds
line	<str>I spoke to Farmer Bea south west of the Digsite and agreed to help her set up her Bee Farm.</str>
line	<str>The bee dealer gave me a box of bees. I should transport them safely back to Farmer Bea at her farm west of The Digsite.</str>
line	<str>At Bea's request, I travelled to the Grand Exchange in Varrock and collected some Bees from a Bee Dealer there. I then carefully delivered them to Bea. However, upon taking them to her hives, we discovered them to actually be Wasps.</str>
line	<str>Bea asked me to thin down the number of Wasps by catching 50 of them. I did so and gathered 50 Wasp Stings in the process. However, the infestation of Wasps lured some Honey Buzzards to the area.</str>
line	<col=000080><col=800000>Bea</col> asked me to thin down the number of <col=800000>Honey Buzzards</col> by catching at least 5 of them and collecting 50 of their feathers. If needed, <col=800000>Bea</col> can give me some equipment that I can use for catching them.</col>
step	6	-	Delivering the feathers
line	<str>I spoke to Farmer Bea south west of the Digsite and agreed to help her set up her Bee Farm.</str>
line	<str>The bee dealer gave me a box of bees. I should transport them safely back to Farmer Bea at her farm west of The Digsite.</str>
line	<str>At Bea's request, I travelled to the Grand Exchange in Varrock and collected some Bees from a Bee Dealer there. I then carefully delivered them to Bea. However, upon taking them to her hives, we discovered them to actually be Wasps.</str>
line	<str>Bea asked me to thin down the number of Wasps by catching 50 of them. I did so and gathered 50 Wasp Stings in the process. However, the infestation of Wasps lured some Honey Buzzards to the area.</str>
line	<col=000080><col=800000>Bea</col> asked me to thin down the number of <col=800000>Honey Buzzards</col> by catching at least 5 of them and collecting 50 of their feathers. Having done that, I should speak to <col=800000>Bea</col> again.</col>
step	7	-	Fletching wasp darts
line	<str>I spoke to Farmer Bea south west of the Digsite and agreed to help her set up her Bee Farm.</str>
line	<str>The bee dealer gave me a box of bees. I should transport them safely back to Farmer Bea at her farm west of The Digsite.</str>
line	<str>At Bea's request, I travelled to the Grand Exchange in Varrock and collected some Bees from a Bee Dealer there. I then carefully delivered them to Bea. However, upon taking them to her hives, we discovered them to actually be Wasps.</str>
line	<str>Bea asked me to thin down the number of Wasps by catching 50 of them. I did so and gathered 50 Wasp Stings in the process. However, the infestation of Wasps lured some Honey Buzzards to the area.</str>
line	<str>Bea asked me to thin down the number of Honey Buzzards by catching at least 5 of them and collecting 50 of their feathers. With that done, Bea once again attempted to move some Bees into her hives. However, it seems the Bee Dealer lied for a second time. The end result was that there were two different types of Wasps and two different types of Honey Buzzard preying on them.</str>
line	<col=000080>To make the best out of a bad situation, <col=800000>Bea</col> has asked me to see if I can make anything out of the <col=800000>Wasp Stings</col> and <col=800000>Feathers</col> I gathered.</col>
step	8	-	Delivering the wasp darts
line	<str>I spoke to Farmer Bea south west of the Digsite and agreed to help her set up her Bee Farm.</str>
line	<str>The bee dealer gave me a box of bees. I should transport them safely back to Farmer Bea at her farm west of The Digsite.</str>
line	<str>At Bea's request, I travelled to the Grand Exchange in Varrock and collected some Bees from a Bee Dealer there. I then carefully delivered them to Bea. However, upon taking them to her hives, we discovered them to actually be Wasps.</str>
line	<str>Bea asked me to thin down the number of Wasps by catching 50 of them. I did so and gathered 50 Wasp Stings in the process. However, the infestation of Wasps lured some Honey Buzzards to the area.</str>
line	<str>Bea asked me to thin down the number of Honey Buzzards by catching at least 5 of them and collecting 50 of their feathers. With that done, Bea once again attempted to move some Bees into her hives. However, it seems the Bee Dealer lied for a second time. The end result was that there were two different types of Wasps and two different types of Honey Buzzard preying on them.</str>
line	<col=000080>To make the best out of a bad situation, <col=800000>Bea</col> asked me to see if I could make anything out of the <col=800000>Wasp Stings</col> and <col=800000>Feathers</col> I gathered. I was able to use them to make some <col=800000>Darts</col>. I should discuss this with <col=800000>Bea</col>.</col>
